{"school":{"dbn":"06M223","name":"The Mott Hall School","boro":"Manhattan","district":"06","district_label":"District 6","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":317,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"401 W. 164th Street, MANHATTAN, NY 10032","phone":"9175212060","website":"http://www.themotthall.org/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63786","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Founded in 1985 as a magnet school for gifted children, the Mott Hall School has long been a source of pride for District Six. MHS is dedicated to the academic and personal development of our students who will become tomorrow's leaders. Our mission is to develop future leaders in Mathematics, Science, and Technology by providing a world-class education that prepares students for college and higher learning. We provide a rigorous academic curriculum that includes experiences both inside and outside the school building. MHS creates a \u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009chome away from home\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009d atmosphere that inspires students to explore, grow, and ask questions. We provide an advanced curriculum with opportunities to earn high school credits by the end of their eighth grade year. Focusing on restorative practices, we also strive to create an atmosphere that moves our students toward assuming personal and social responsibility. We work closely with community partners, including our treasured partnerships with National Dance Institute and City College, to provide a well-rounded, \u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009cschool without walls\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009d learning experience for all of our scholars.","start_time":"07:44am","end_time":"02:05pm","languages":null,"subway":"1 to 168th St; A to 168t